Example 3 : Find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 2 integers m and n. 
Apply Euclid's algorithm by repeatedly subtracting the smaller number from the larger number until the 2
numbers are equal, which is then the GCD. In the program, we convention that m is the larger number and n is the smaller
number. Add an auxiliary variable r to compute the difference between the 2 numbers. Then reassign m or n to r such that m >
n and repeat. The loop stops when m = n. 
void main() 
{ 
int m, n, r; 
cout << "Nh ậ p m, n: " ; cin >> m >> n ; 
if (m < n) { int t = m; m = n; n = t; }   // if m < n, swap the roles of the two numbers 
while (m != n) { 
r = m - n ; 
if (r > n) m = r; else { m = n ; n = r ; } 
} 
cout << "UCLN = " << m ; 
} 
