c. Drawing lines and polylines 
• line(x1, y1, x2, y2): Draws a line from (x1, y1) to (x2, y2). The screen cursor remains at its old position. 
• lineto(x, y): Draws a line from the current cursor position to position (x, y). The cursor moves to (x, y). 
• linerel(dx, dy): Let (x, y) be the current cursor position; this command will draw a line connecting (x, y) to a new point with coordinates (x+dx, y+dy). That is, this command is also equivalent to the command lineto(getx()+dx, gety()+dy), where getx() and gety() are two functions returning the current x, y position of the cursor. After execution, the linerel command will place the cursor at the end position of the newly drawn line. 
