IV. CONSTRUCTOR 
1. Constructor 
A constructor is also a method of a class (but a special function) used to construct a new object. The compiler will allocate memory for the object and then call the constructor. The constructor will initialize values for the object's attributes and can perform some other tasks to prepare the new object. 
a. How to write a constructor 
i. Differences between a constructor and normal methods: 
When writing a constructor, note 3 differences of a constructor compared to other methods as follows: 
• Name of the constructor: The name of the constructor must match the name of the class. 
• Do not declare a return type for the constructor. 
• The constructor does not have a return value. 
ii. Similarities between a constructor and normal methods 
Besides the 3 differences above, a constructor is written like other methods: 
• A constructor can be defined inside or outside the class definition. 
