To make function f a friend of classes A, B, and C, we use the following template:
class A;   // Forward declaration of class A
class B;   // Forward declaration of class B
class C;   // Forward declaration of class C
// Definition of class A
class A
{
// Declare f as a friend of A
friend void f(...) ; 
} ; 
// Definition of class B
class B
{
// Declare f as a friend of B
friend void f(...) ; 
} ; 
// Definition of class C
class C
{
// Declare f as a friend of C
friend void f(...) ; 
} ; 
// Implement function f
void f(...)
{
...
}
