V. BINARY INPUT/OUTPUT 
1.   Concepts of 2 file types: text and binary 
a.   Text files 
In a text file, each byte is treated as a character. However, if 2 bytes 10
(LF), 13 (CR) are consecutive, they are considered as a single character, which is the newline character. Thus, 
a text file is a set of lines of characters with the newline character having the code 10. The character 
with code 26 is considered the end-of-file character. 
