evaluates to   4   (2 + 2) if the left operand ( ++i ) is evaluated first and evaluates to   3 
(2   +   1) if the right operand ( i ) is evaluated first.
Since C++ cannot guarantee the operand evaluation order, you should not write code
that depends on the operand evaluation order. 
