+ ,   2 ,   ) ,   * ,   4 ,   - , and   3 .
The   evaluateExpression   function scans each token in the   for   loop (lines 77–122).
If a token is an operand, push it to   operandStack   (line 120). If a token is a   +   or   –   operator
