Caution 
If a class is designed to be extended, it is better to provide a   no-arg constructor   to avoid
programming errors. Consider the following code: 
class   Fruit
{ 
public :
Fruit( int   id)
{
}
}; 
class   Apple:   public   Fruit
{ 
public :
Apple()
{
}
